        "body": {
         "type": "doc",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "attrs": {
            "align": null
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "text": "Establish the Testing Environment:",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "strong"
              },
              {
               "type": "em"
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "bullet_list",
           "content": [
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Say: ",
                 "type": "text"
                },
                {
                 "text": "Today you will demonstrate what you have learned during the first investigation of this unit. Your goal is to see how well you can apply your skills to new texts.",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "textColor",
                   "attrs": {
                    "color": "#45818e"
                   }
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "heading",
           "attrs": {
            "align": null,
            "level": 3
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "text": "TEI Format Guide & Rubric",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "strong"
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "attrs": {
            "align": null
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "text": "How to complete the TEI formats:",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "strong"
              },
              {
               "type": "em"
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "bullet_list",
           "content": [
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Multiple Choice (MC): ",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": "For these items, choose the one answer that best matches the question. Read all four choices carefully before selecting your answer.",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Fill-in-the-Blank (FITB):",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " For these items, you will write the word you hear on the line provided. Listen carefully as the word is read, then used in a sentence, then repeated. Spell the word as accurately as you can.",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Multiple Select (MS):",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " \"For these items, there is more than one correct answer. The question will usually tell you to 'Select ",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": "two",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": "' or ask 'Which ",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": "three",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " statements...' If you only pick one, the item will not be fully correct.\"",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Sorting/Matching:",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " \"You will see a list of details and two categories (Passage 1 and Passage 2). You must click and drag each detail into the correct box based on which author emphasized that point. Note: Some details might fit both, but choose the primary emphasis.\"",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Sequencing/Ordering:",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " \"For the timeline or logical flow questions, you must drag the events into the correct chronological order as described in the text. Pay close attention to transition words like 'subsequently' or 'initially'.\"",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        "title": "Launch",
        "purpose": {
         "type": "doc",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "attrs": {
            "align": null
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "text": "The teacher will establish the testing environment for students to take their assessment.",
             "type": "text"
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        "audience": "teacher",
        "sequence": 1,
        "estimated_time_in_minutes": [
         5,
         5
        ]
       },
       {
        "body": {
         "type": "doc",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "attrs": {
            "align": null
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "text": "Assessment Time!",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "strong"
              },
              {
               "type": "em"
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "attrs": {
            "align": null
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "text": "Provide students with access to the ",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "em"
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "text": "Unit 2 Investigation 2 Assessment ",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "strong"
              },
              {
               "type": "em"
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "text": "and walk them through the expectations.",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "em"
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "attrs": {
            "align": null
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "text": "Active Monitoring Notes",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "strong"
              },
              {
               "type": "em"
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "attrs": {
            "align": null
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "text": "During the assessment, look for:",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "em"
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "bullet_list",
           "content": [
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "TEI Troubleshooting:",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " Watch for students who select only one answer on a Multiple Select item instead of selecting two responses.",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Pacing:",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " Ensure students without extended time accommodations have moved on to Passage 2 by the halfway mark (20 minutes), as the cross-text items at the end require knowledge of both passages.",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Spelling Administration:",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " For Items 20–23, read each word aloud, read the sentence, then repeat the word in a measured, neutral tone. Do not segment the word, over-enunciate sound patterns, or signal correctness. In digital administration, confirm that students can access the audio as intended.",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "collapsible",
           "attrs": {
            "label": "Integrated ELD Instructions"
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "type": "callout",
             "attrs": {
              "variant": "purpose"
             },
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "To provide equitable access to complex literary texts and multi-step assessment items, ensuring that linguistic barriers do not impede a student's ability to demonstrate mastery of standards.",
                 "type": "text"
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "For students requiring offline accommodations, provide a human reader. The reader must deliver the text, stems, and options at a measured, neutral pace without using inflection or tone to emphasize correct answers or suggest meaning.",
                 "type": "text"
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "For students with Extended Time, provide a quiet transition for them to continue working while others move to the Look Back.",
                 "type": "text"
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Focus facilitation on stems with dense academic wording, especially items asking students to identify what best supports an idea, how the author most effectively develops contrasting perspectives, or what a word most nearly means in context.",
                 "type": "text"
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Encourage students to annotate passages in any language.",
                 "type": "text"
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Affirm that English Learners bring cross-linguistic knowledge that supports comprehension of complex texts.",
                 "type": "text"
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Remind students: You know more than you think. Trust your reading.",
                 "type": "text"
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "paragraph",
             "attrs": {
              "align": null
             },
             "content": [
              {
               "text": "🛠️ TEACHER MOVES",
